# Local development only (`pnpm everyapp dev`). Copy to .dev.vars; never commit it.
# Deployed, the app has no secrets: the gateway holds every key.
#
# AI: the app calls models through the gateway's AI proxy. With no gateway in
# development, the SDK calls a provider directly with a key here (billed to
# you).
#
# The default (AI_PROVIDER unset): the Gateway's default model, which the SDK
# resolves on this file in the Gateway's order, OpenRouter first. That needs
# everyapp and @every-app/sdk 0.3.0-rc.2 or later: 0.3.0-rc.1 refuses the
# manifest's ai.chat and its local fallback doesn't serve the default route,
# so on rc.1 run with a pin instead (AI_PROVIDER=openrouter pnpm everyapp dev,
# or AI_PROVIDER=workers-ai) and that provider's key below. A pin works the
# same on rc.2.
#
# OpenRouter: a key from https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
#
# Or Workers AI: an API token made from the "Workers AI" template (Workers AI
# Read and Edit) and its account id.
# WORKERS_AI_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
#
# Email: the SDK checks each send against EVERYAPP_EMAIL_SENDERS and prints
# it. With all three of EMAIL_REST_API_TOKEN, CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID (above)
# and EMAIL_FROM it sends through the Email Sending REST API instead, on your
# account. Set EVERYAPP_EMAIL_SENDERS for the mailbox domains, and EMAIL_FROM
# for GET /api/v1/config to say ready: true.
# EVERYAPP_EMAIL_SENDERS=["*@example.com"]
# EMAIL_REST_API_TOKEN=
# EMAIL_FROM=
# EMAIL_FROM_NAME=
